      {
        "id": "p9-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Calculate the area of this rectangle, giving answer in $\\text{cm}^{2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$21\\text{ cm}^{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*} A &= 7\\times3\\text{ cm}^{2} \\\\ A &= 21\\text{ cm}^{2} \\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Convert your answer to $\\text{mm}^{2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2100\\text{ mm}^{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*} 1\\text{ cm}^{2} &= 10^{2}\\text{ mm}^{2} \\\\ 21\\text{ cm}^{2} &= 21\\times10^{2}\\text{ mm}^{2} \\\\ 21\\text{ cm}^{2} &= 2100\\text{ mm}^{2} \\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Redo the calculation by first converting $3\\text{ cm}$ and $7\\text{ cm}$ to mm, then calculate the area, giving answer in $\\text{mm}^{2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2100\\text{ mm}^{2}$; use $30\\text{ mm}\\times70\\text{ mm}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*} 3\\text{ cm} &= 30\\text{ mm} \\\\ 7\\text{ cm} &= 70\\text{ mm} \\\\ A &= 30\\times70\\text{ mm}^{2} \\\\ A &= 2100\\text{ mm}^{2} \\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "When doing area calculations, does it matter if you first convert the lengths or convert the area at the end? Which do you prefer?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Both methods give the same area when used correctly. Preference varies; Mr Ding recommends converting lengths first to reduce area-conversion mistakes.",
          "worked": "Both methods give the same area because the area conversion factor is the square of the length conversion factor.\n\n$$\\begin{align*} A &= (3\\times7)\\times10^{2}\\text{ mm}^{2} = 2100\\text{ mm}^{2} \\\\ A &= (3\\times10)(7\\times10)\\text{ mm}^{2} = 2100\\text{ mm}^{2} \\end{align*}$$\n\nPreference varies. For example, I prefer converting lengths first. Mr Ding recommends this approach because students tend to make mistakes converting units of area.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ],
    "diagramPlacement": "right-of-prompt"
  },
